[lib/internal/encoding/single-byte.js] The character tables should probably be pollution-protected.


```suggestion
const e = (length) => new SafeArrayIterator(ArrayFrom({ length }, () => 1));
const z = (length) => new SafeArrayIterator(ArrayFrom({ length }, () => 0));
```

[lib/internal/encoding/single-byte.js] Also:

```suggestion
const e = (length) => ArrayPrototypeFill(new Array(length), 1);
const z = (length) => ArrayPrototypeFill(new Array(length), 0);
```

is significantly faster than `Array.from()`.

[lib/internal/encoding/single-byte.js] ```suggestion
  const incomplete = TypedArrayPrototypeIncludes(map, 0xfffd);
```

[lib/internal/encoding/single-byte.js] ```suggestion
    const b = new FastBuffer(o.buffer, o.byteOffset, o.byteLength);
```

[lib/internal/encoding.js] ```suggestion
      return new FastBuffer(input);
```

[lib/internal/encoding.js] ```suggestion
      return new FastBuffer(input.buffer, input.byteOffset, input.byteLength);
```

[lib/internal/encoding/single-byte.js] ```suggestion
  map.set(TypedArrayFrom(Uint16Array, new SafeArrayIterator(encodings[encoding]), (x) => (prev += x)), 128);
```

[lib/internal/encoding/single-byte.js] Nit: The callback variant of the arrayish `.from` methods is really quite slow. It's significantly quicker to create an empty typed array and fill the desired portion using a simple loop.

```suggestion
  const map = new Uint16Array(256);
  // Populate the ASCII region
  for (let i = 0; i < 128; i++) {
    map[i] = i;
  }
```

[lib/internal/encoding/single-byte.js] Nit: Again, a loop here is much faster than passing a callback to `.from()`.


```suggestion
  const offsets = encodings[encoding];
  for (let i = 128; i < 256; i++) {
    const x = offsets[i];
    map[i] = x === r ? r : (prev += x);
  }
```

[lib/internal/encoding/single-byte.js] Nit: Again, much faster to do the following:

```suggestion
    const map = new Uint16Array(256);
    for (let i = 0; i < 128; i++) {
      map[i] = i;
    }
    for (let i = 128; i < 256; i++) {
      map[i] = i + 0xf700;
    }
    return map;
```

