'use strict';
// Flags: --expose-internals
```

[test/parallel/test-parse-args.mjs] We should always check strings first, as `1 is not equal to 0` does very little to help with debugging.
```suggestion
        assert.deepStrictEqual(JSON.parse(stdout), { foo: true, bar: true });
        assert.strictEqual(stderr, '');
        assert.strictEqual(code, 0);
        assert.strictEqual(signal, null);
```
Alternatively, we can use `deepStrictEqual` to test everything at once:
```suggestion
        assert.deepStrictEqual({
          code,
          signal,
          stderr,
          stdout: JSON.parse(stdout),
        }, {
          code: 0,
          signal: null,
          stderr: '',
          stdout: { foo: true, bar: true },
        });
```

